关于韩剧的内容也是他即兴发挥的吗？

1175
00:57:53.170 --> 00:57:54.950
No, that was all scripted.
不，那全是剧本写好的。

1176
00:57:55.190 --> 00:57:55.710
Wow.
哇。

1177
00:57:56.150 --> 00:57:56.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1178
00:57:56.790 --> 00:58:00.050
Well, none of this girl talk is helping Pam get to the bottom of things.
好吧，这些闺蜜谈话对帕姆查明真相一点帮助都没有。

1179
00:58:00.270 --> 00:58:00.590
No.
没有。

1180
00:58:00.690 --> 00:58:02.330
It's been completely derailed.
完全跑题了。

1181
00:58:02.830 --> 00:58:06.190
This girl talk in the break room scene actually was extended.
休息室里的这段闺蜜谈话其实被延长了。

1182
00:58:06.390 --> 00:58:07.990
It had a whole second beat.
它还有完整的一段后续。

1183
00:58:08.210 --> 00:58:09.210
It's in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里有。

1184
00:58:09.210 --> 00:58:11.070
It's also in deleted scenes.
删减片段里也有。

1185
00:58:11.930 --> 00:58:13.690
Daryl is going to join the party.
达里尔也要加入这场聚会。

1186
00:58:13.870 --> 00:58:15.570
But it's not why you think.
但原因和你想象的不一样。

1187
00:58:15.570 --> 00:58:19.310
We find out that he has a little friend that lives in the break room.
我们发现他在休息室里养了个小宠物。

1188
00:58:19.550 --> 00:58:20.750
I want you to hear it.
我想让你们听听看。

1189
00:58:20.750 --> 00:58:25.430
I keep asking myself, what is my skinny girl margarita?
我一直在问自己，我的“瘦身玛格丽特”是什么？

1190
00:58:26.190 --> 00:58:31.410
I think we should all go around in a circle and each tell one secret, except for Gabe.
我觉得我们应该围成一圈，每个人分享一个秘密，盖博除外。

1191
00:58:31.970 --> 00:58:33.050
Let's go around here.
我们围过来吧。

1192
00:58:34.510 --> 00:58:36.370
What, is everyone just hanging out?
怎么了，大家都在这儿闲逛吗？

1193
00:58:36.550 --> 00:58:38.330
No, we're letting it all hang out.
不，我们是在敞开心扉。

1194
00:58:38.970 --> 00:58:40.270
Nellie was going to tell a story.
奈莉本来要讲个故事。

1195
00:58:40.270 --> 00:58:41.770
Oh, great.
哦，太棒了。

1196
00:58:41.910 --> 00:58:42.510
Sounds good.
听起来不错。

1197
00:58:43.170 --> 00:58:44.390
Break room's busy today.
休息室今天真热闹。

1198
00:58:45.570 --> 00:58:46.450
Nobody knows.
没人知道。

1199
00:58:46.710 --> 00:58:49.190
There's a mouse who lives in the wall behind the vending machine.
自动售货机后面的墙里住着一只老鼠。

1200
00:58:49.570 --> 00:58:50.470
I feed him.
我在喂它。

1201
00:58:50.650 --> 00:58:52.550
Now he comes out every day at the same time.
现在他每天都在同一时间出来。

1202
00:58:53.050 --> 00:58:55.130
If people find Squeaker, he's toaSt.
如果被别人发现“吱吱”，他就死定了。

1203
00:58:55.510 --> 00:58:57.050
I just want to give him his food.
我只是想给他喂点吃的。

1204
00:58:57.830 --> 00:58:59.570
And try one more time with the top hat.
再试一次戴高帽子的戏。

1205
00:59:01.570 --> 00:59:04.970
He's trying to put a top hat on a little mouse named Squeaker?
他想给一只叫“吱吱”的小老鼠戴高帽子？

1206
00:59:05.330 --> 00:59:07.750
Yes, and he holds up the top hat.
对，他举着那顶高帽子。

1207
00:59:07.910 --> 00:59:12.250
And you know, Craig Robinson has big hands and he holds up a tiny top hat.
你知道的，克雷格·罗宾逊的手很大，他举着一顶微型高帽子。

1208
00:59:12.250 --> 00:59:13.350
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1209
00:59:13.430 --> 00:59:15.430
A tiny top hat for a little mouse.
给小老鼠戴的微型高帽子。

1210
00:59:15.570 --> 00:59:15.990
Yes.
没错。

1211
00:59:16.190 --> 00:59:20.930
And then there was a whole other scene where we find out that Erin has also been feeding
还有另一场戏，我们发现艾琳也一直在休息室里

1212
00:59:20.930 --> 00:59:22.790
a mouse in the break room.
喂一只老鼠。

1213
00:59:23.110 --> 00:59:24.610
She doesn't call it Squeaker.
她不叫它“吱吱”。

1214
00:59:24.770 --> 00:59:29.590
She says it's like multiple generations in a family she's been feeding for a while.
她说那是一个老鼠家族，好几代了，她喂了有一阵子了。

1215
00:59:29.590 --> 00:59:32.930
And then Daryl's like, how many of these mice are there?
然后达里尔就问，到底有多少只老鼠？

1216
00:59:33.010 --> 00:59:33.990
And she's like, oh, hundreds.
她说，哦，几百只吧。

1217
00:59:34.330 --> 00:59:35.770
And now Daryl's like, oh, no.
达里尔听了就觉得，噢，不。

1218
00:59:36.030 --> 00:59:36.470
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1219
00:59:36.730 --> 00:59:37.550
Pump the brakes.
打住，慢着。

1220
00:59:37.590 --> 00:59:38.450
What's happening?
怎么回事？

1221
00:59:38.830 --> 00:59:40.630
But I did love this callback.
但我真的很喜欢这个呼应。

1222
00:59:40.790 --> 00:59:45.970
I pointed it out to Warren and Halstead that Daryl has a soft spot for little creatures.
我跟沃伦和霍尔斯特德提过，达里尔对小动物心肠很软。

1223
00:59:46.010 --> 00:59:49.350
Remember in Fun Run where he's feeding the squirrel in the parking lot?
还记得在《趣味跑》里，他在停车场喂松鼠吗？

1224
00:59:49.750 --> 00:59:50.270
Oh, yeah.
噢，记得。

1225
00:59:50.630 --> 00:59:50.930
Yeah.
对。

1226
00:59:51.510 --> 00:59:55.670
Well, speaking of creatures, we're heading...
话说回来，说到动物，我们要去……

1227
00:59:55.670 --> 00:59:56.150
What is this segue?
这是什么转折？

1228
00:59:56.150 --> 01:00:01.710
Yeah, well, we're heading back to Prestige because Andy is speaking to Mr. Romish.
好吧，我们要回到Prestige公司，因为安迪正在和罗米什先生谈话。

1229
01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:02.470
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

1230
01:00:02.750 --> 01:00:08.190
And I realized I have not done a location breakdown of Prestige Direct Mail Solutions.
我意识到我还没做过Prestige直邮解决方案公司的场景拆解。

1231
01:00:08.810 --> 01:00:11.690
How does a creature come into this location breakdown?
这跟动物有什么关系？

1232
01:00:12.050 --> 01:00:13.070
I will tell you.
我这就告诉你。

1233
01:00:13.310 --> 01:00:17.750
Dani shared that they did a big location scout for this episode because they wanted to find
丹妮分享说，他们为这一集做了大规模的取景勘察，因为他们想找

1234
01:00:17.750 --> 01:00:25.090
one location that could be used for the interior offices of Prestige, but also for the lobby
一个既能作为Prestige内部办公室，又能作为大厅

1235
01:00:25.090 --> 01:00:28.830
and elevator scenes and the exterior scenes, including the coffee cart.
和电梯场景，以及包括咖啡车在内的外景拍摄地。

1236
01:00:28.950 --> 01:00:30.070
All of that is coming up.
这些稍后都会提到。

1237
01:00:30.330 --> 01:00:33.110
He said they had to look at a few different office buildings.
他说他们看了好几栋不同的办公楼。

1238
01:00:33.110 --> 01:00:40.950
One of them was a vacant office in the valley, but in the middle of the lobby, there was this
其中一栋是山谷里的一间空办公室，但在大厅中央，有一个

1239
01:00:40.950 --> 01:00:45.850
big sort of seemingly abandoned fish tank in there.
看起来像是被遗弃的大鱼缸。

1240
01:00:46.030 --> 01:00:49.970
It was really super cloudy and the glass had algae on it.
水非常浑浊，玻璃上还长满了藻类。

1241
01:00:50.570 --> 01:00:54.430
But inside the tank, there was an arowana fish.
但鱼缸里有一条龙鱼。

1242
01:00:55.190 --> 01:01:00.190
I guess it's a pretty large fish that lives in the Amazon.
我猜那是一种生活在亚马逊河的大型鱼类。

1243
01:01:01.270 --> 01:01:06.210
And Dani said it was just in there and it was alone.
丹妮说它就待在里面，孤零零的。

1244
01:01:06.690 --> 01:01:08.370
I feel bad for it.
我真为它感到难过。

1245
01:01:08.470 --> 01:01:09.090
I know.
我也是。

1246
01:01:09.390 --> 01:01:13.350
You know, Dani wondered, like, who was caring for this?
你知道，丹妮当时就在想，到底是谁在照顾它？

1247
01:01:13.890 --> 01:01:15.790
Was anyone caring for it?
有人在照顾它吗？

1248
01:01:16.090 --> 01:01:18.190
Ultimately, they didn't pick that location.
最终，他们没有选那个地方。

1249
01:01:19.410 --> 01:01:26.710
Incidentally, the United States banned the ownership of arowanas because they're an endangered species.
顺便说一下，美国禁止饲养龙鱼，因为它们是濒危物种。

1250
01:01:27.390 --> 01:01:29.710
Yeah, I was going to say, is that even legal?
是啊，我正想说，这合法吗？

1251
01:01:30.310 --> 01:01:32.130
I don't think so.
我不这么认为。

1252
01:01:32.430 --> 01:01:34.770
What does an arowana look like?
龙鱼长什么样？

1253
01:01:35.210 --> 01:01:36.990
They're very big.
它们非常大。

1254
01:01:37.510 --> 01:01:39.450
Okay, big, check.
好吧，很大，记下了。

1255
01:01:39.450 --> 01:01:47.310
They're sort of, some of them, when I looked at pictures, they have like, they can have
它们有点，我看照片的时候，它们有，它们可以有

1256
01:01:47.310 --> 01:01:49.930
sort of like an orangey glow.
一种橙色的光泽。

1257
01:01:50.130 --> 01:01:52.390
Others are kind of a yellowy glow.
其他的则是一种偏黄的光泽。

1258
01:01:53.370 --> 01:01:54.850
God, what do they look like?
天哪，它们到底长什么样？

1259
01:01:54.930 --> 01:01:57.010
They have sort of like a mouth that.
它们的嘴巴有点像。

1260
01:01:57.430 --> 01:01:59.050
Does it come up from under?
是从下面长上来的吗？

1261
01:01:59.250 --> 01:01:59.910
It comes up.
它是从下面长上来的。

1262
01:01:59.910 --> 01:02:00.850
Is that why you're doing that?
这就是你刚才那样做的原因吗？

1263
01:02:01.610 --> 01:02:02.130
Yes.
是的。

1264
01:02:02.670 --> 01:02:04.550
It comes up from under.
它是从下面长上来的。

1265
01:02:05.170 --> 01:02:07.450
Like a big old mouth from under.
就像一张从下面长出来的大嘴。

1266
01:02:07.450 --> 01:02:12.470
I couldn't see your face just in that one moment because I was Googling what they look like.
刚才那一瞬间我没看你的脸，因为我在谷歌搜索它们长什么样。

1267
01:02:12.630 --> 01:02:16.750
But I could tell from your character what you were doing.
但我从你的动作就能看出你在做什么。

1268
01:02:17.190 --> 01:02:17.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1269
01:02:17.890 --> 01:02:21.270
And then their eyes look kind of.
然后它们的眼睛看起来有点。

1270
01:02:21.870 --> 01:02:24.770
Okay, listen, we don't have to describe this fish anymore.
好了，听着，我们不用再描述这条鱼了。

1271
01:02:25.030 --> 01:02:25.890
We can let it go.
我们可以跳过这个话题。

1272
01:02:26.070 --> 01:02:28.090
But we'll put a picture in stories.
不过我们会把照片发到快拍里。

1273
01:02:28.510 --> 01:02:28.950
Sure.
没问题。

1274
01:02:29.190 --> 01:02:32.790
So anyway, that was my segue about strange creatures.
总之，这就是我关于奇怪生物的过渡话题。

1275
01:02:32.790 --> 01:02:37.870
Steve Burgess told me that ultimately we filmed at the Borax building in Valencia.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，我们最终是在瓦伦西亚的硼砂大楼拍摄的。

1276
01:02:38.150 --> 01:02:39.230
Minus the fish.
没有鱼的那种。

1277
01:02:39.590 --> 01:02:41.370
Yeah, there was no fish at this location.
对，这个拍摄地点没有鱼。

1278
01:02:41.530 --> 01:02:47.550
And they spent all day shooting at this location, which, Angela, means we had a day off.
他们在那儿拍了一整天，安吉拉，这意味着我们那天休息。

1279
01:02:48.130 --> 01:02:48.570
Hope.
希望如此。

1280
01:02:49.590 --> 01:02:53.830
Andy's about to win a big old client for his new company, Big Red.
安迪正要为他的新公司“大红”争取到一个大客户。

1281
01:02:53.830 --> 01:02:58.210
Instead, he tells Mr. Ramesh that Prestige will get 100% of his attention.
结果他告诉拉梅什先生，Prestige公司会百分之百关注他的需求。

1282
01:02:58.750 --> 01:03:01.710
He can save him 25% on his costs.
他能帮他节省25%的成本。

1283
01:03:01.970 --> 01:03:05.430
He's going to give him his personal phone number and a key to his house.
他还要把自己的私人电话号码和家里的钥匙给他。

1284
01:03:05.710 --> 01:03:06.190
Yeah.
没错。

1285
01:03:06.510 --> 01:03:09.110
And his internet password, which is Eat, Pray, Love.
还有他的上网密码，是“饭祷爱”。

1286
01:03:09.490 --> 01:03:13.830
Where is Andy getting this paper from that he's now going to give to him?
安迪现在要给他的这些文件是从哪儿弄来的？

1287
01:03:13.830 --> 01:03:15.270
He's going to figure that out later.
他打算回头再想办法。

1288
01:03:15.470 --> 01:03:17.410
He's faking it till he can make it.
他这是在装模作样，直到成功为止。

1289
01:03:17.650 --> 01:03:17.950
Right.
对。

1290
01:03:17.950 --> 01:03:20.090
But he wins over Mr. Ramesh.
但他还是赢得了拉梅什先生的信任。

1291
01:03:20.450 --> 01:03:24.190
Well, meanwhile, Jim and Dwight arrive at the Prestige headquarters.
与此同时，吉姆和德怀特到达了Prestige总部。

1292
01:03:24.650 --> 01:03:26.050
They run in.
他们跑了进去。

1293
01:03:26.210 --> 01:03:28.290
They try to lock the door.
他们试图锁上门。

1294
01:03:28.550 --> 01:03:30.310
Yeah, they don't want Harry to come in.
对，他们不想让哈里进来。

1295
01:03:30.490 --> 01:03:31.750
Dwight takes off his belt.
德怀特解下了他的皮带。

1296
01:03:32.030 --> 01:03:38.130
You know, he's thinking in the moment and kind of makes some kind of knot ties the door shut.
你知道，他当时灵机一动，打了个结把门拴住了。

1297
01:03:38.130 --> 01:03:39.870
But now his pants won't stay up.
但现在他的裤子提不住了。

1298
01:03:40.030 --> 01:03:45.390
I made a mental note of this moment because I thought if I'm ever being chased
我记下了这一刻，因为我想如果我哪天被追赶

1299
01:03:45.390 --> 01:03:48.970
or maybe during the zombie apocalypse that I prepped for all the time.
或者是在我一直为之准备的僵尸末日里。

1300
01:03:49.230 --> 01:03:49.570
Sure, sure.
当然，当然。

1301
01:03:49.930 --> 01:03:52.530
That the belt around the door, it was smart.
把皮带系在门把手上，这招很聪明。

1302
01:03:52.790 --> 01:03:56.250
I mean, I know that they can smash the glass and get the belt off,
我是说，我知道他们可以砸碎玻璃把皮带解开，

1303
01:03:56.350 --> 01:03:57.950
but it's definitely going to slow them down.
但这绝对会拖慢他们的速度。

1304
01:03:58.150 --> 01:04:01.790
But then the big problem I had was I don't ever wear a belt.
但我遇到的最大问题是我从来不系皮带。

1305
01:04:02.210 --> 01:04:03.590
Yeah, well, there's the problem.
是啊，问题就在这儿。

1306
01:04:03.850 --> 01:04:07.430
And it made me wonder if I should be wearing.
这让我怀疑自己是不是该系上皮带。

1307
01:04:07.430 --> 01:04:07.950
Take your bra off.
把你的胸罩脱下来。

1308
01:04:07.950 --> 01:04:08.650
Oh, oh.
噢，噢。

1309
01:04:08.650 --> 01:04:09.910
Take your bra off.
把你的胸罩脱下来。

1310
01:04:09.970 --> 01:04:10.390
Yes.
没错。

1311
01:04:10.730 --> 01:04:13.450
Tie that sucker around there a few times.
把它在那儿缠上几圈。

1312
01:04:13.730 --> 01:04:14.150
Yes.
对。

1313
01:04:14.650 --> 01:04:16.830
When am I going to see that in a zombie movie?
我什么时候才能在僵尸电影里看到这一幕？

1314
01:04:17.050 --> 01:04:17.770
That's brilliant.
这太天才了。

1315
01:04:18.130 --> 01:04:18.930
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1316
01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:22.590
Gals, we can take that off so fast through the armpit of your shirt.
姑娘们，我们可以直接从衬衫袖口把它迅速脱下来。

1317
01:04:22.790 --> 01:04:23.450
We've all done it.
我们都干过这事儿。

1318
01:04:23.590 --> 01:04:25.210
Don't even have to take your shirt off.
甚至都不用脱掉衬衫。

1319
01:04:25.470 --> 01:04:25.870
No.
没错。

1320
01:04:26.190 --> 01:04:26.670
Mm-mm.
嗯。

1321
01:04:27.190 --> 01:04:28.250
That's so smart.
这太聪明了。

1322
01:04:29.470 --> 01:04:32.170
Someone, please file that away as a plot point.
哪位编剧，请把这个情节记下来。

1323
01:04:32.170 --> 01:04:32.290
I'm ready.
我准备好了。

1324
01:04:32.570 --> 01:04:32.890
I'm ready.
我准备好了。

1325
01:04:33.110 --> 01:04:35.250
In a future film or for your real life.
不管是为以后的电影还是为了你的现实生活。

1326
01:04:35.690 --> 01:04:38.110
So anyway, Dwight's pants are falling down.
总之，德怀特的裤子快掉下来了。

1327
01:04:38.110 --> 01:04:39.590
He runs into the elevator.
他跑进了电梯。

1328
01:04:40.130 --> 01:04:41.270
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1329
01:04:41.270 --> 01:04:46.490
But clearly there are other doors to this building because Harry runs into the elevator with them.
显然这栋楼还有别的门，因为哈里和他们一起跑进了电梯。

1330
01:04:47.070 --> 01:04:50.670
But as the doors are closing, Dwight presses a different floor.
但就在电梯门关上的时候，德怀特按了另一个楼层。

1331
01:04:51.170 --> 01:04:52.850
He forces Jim out.
他强行把吉姆推了出去。

1332
01:04:52.990 --> 01:04:54.310
He's like, meet me upstairs.
他说，去楼上找我。

1333
01:04:54.510 --> 01:04:55.190
Run upstairs.
跑去楼上。

1334
01:04:56.990 --> 01:04:57.910
Jim's like, what?
吉姆一脸茫然，什么？

1335
01:04:58.130 --> 01:04:59.330
And he's like, take the stairs.
他说，走楼梯。

1336
01:04:59.490 --> 01:05:01.650
And Jim's like, I don't even know where the stairs are.
吉姆说，我甚至不知道楼梯在哪儿。

1337
01:05:01.650 --> 01:05:08.570
And Dwight starts jumping up and down as hard as he can in the elevator to, what, maybe make it not go?
然后德怀特开始在电梯里拼命蹦跳，是为了什么，让电梯停下吗？

1338
01:05:08.890 --> 01:05:12.170
He wants to activate the seismic fail safe.
他想触发电梯的地震安全机制。

1339
01:05:12.510 --> 01:05:13.250
There it is.
就是这个。

1340
01:05:13.650 --> 01:05:19.270
Well, we asked our director, Danny, which scenes from this episode were special to him, and this was one of them.
我们问了导演丹尼，这一集中哪些场景对他来说很特别，这就是其中之一。

1341
01:05:19.370 --> 01:05:20.370
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1342
01:05:20.370 --> 01:05:25.210
The sequence where they are racing up to the prestige office was the most fun to shoot.
他们冲向普雷斯蒂奇办公室的那段戏拍起来最过瘾。

1343
01:05:25.390 --> 01:05:28.670
It was as close as the office gets to an action sequence.
那是《办公室》里最接近动作戏的片段了。

1344
01:05:28.950 --> 01:05:31.350
Rain and John crushed it as always.
雷恩和约翰一如既往地表现出色。

1345
01:05:31.710 --> 01:05:44.370
The stuff with Dwight tying the door shut with his belt and then having his pants sag then fully fall down while trying to trigger the elevator fail safe was just sublime physical comedy that totally served the story.
德怀特用皮带把门系住，裤子先是松垮，最后在试图触发电梯安全机制时完全掉了下来，这段肢体喜剧简直绝了，而且完全服务于剧情。

1346
01:05:44.370 --> 01:05:57.570
Oh, and he said, also, I remembered BJ's one piece of directing advice was to have one shot that was ambitious or special, and this scene was mine, and it was so much fun.
噢，他还说，我还记得BJ给过我一个导演建议，就是要在片子里安排一个有野心或特别的镜头，这一幕就是我的那个镜头，拍起来太有趣了。

1347
01:05:58.270 --> 01:06:02.530
Yeah, Warren and Halstead also shared about this elevator scene.
没错，沃伦和霍尔斯特德也分享了关于这个电梯场景的看法。

1348
01:06:02.910 --> 01:06:08.430
You know, Warren pointed out that the camera goes into the elevator, and then it stays with Dwight and Harry.
沃伦指出，摄像机进入电梯后，就一直跟着德怀特和哈里。

1349
01:06:08.790 --> 01:06:10.250
Yeah, it's in the corner.
没错，就在角落里。

1350
01:06:10.250 --> 01:06:14.290
Warren said this was one continuous shot in a real elevator.
沃伦说这是一个在真实电梯里拍摄的长镜头。

1351
01:06:14.470 --> 01:06:24.370
There was no fakie elevator here that John really did have to run up a flight of stairs in order to be at the elevator doors when they opened again.
这里并没有什么假电梯，约翰确实得跑上一层楼梯，才能在电梯门再次打开时赶到门口。

1352
01:06:24.370 --> 01:06:26.290
There was no special timing to that.
那并没有什么特别的计时。

1353
01:06:26.730 --> 01:06:27.010
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1354
01:06:27.210 --> 01:06:30.310
He said the stairs were not close either.
他说楼梯离得也不近。

1355
01:06:30.630 --> 01:06:36.510
He said John had to sprint and run up a flight of stairs numerous times.
他说约翰不得不多次冲刺并跑上一层楼梯。

1356
01:06:36.510 --> 01:06:44.370
But Warren said John never complained, but all that sweat and him being out of breath, he said that was real.
但沃伦说约翰从没抱怨过，不过他那一身的汗和气喘吁吁的样子，他说那都是真的。

1357
01:06:44.890 --> 01:06:46.450
It seemed very real.
看起来非常真实。

1358
01:06:46.610 --> 01:06:50.190
When Warren and Halstead shared that with us, I was like, oh, my gosh, I had no idea.
当沃伦和霍尔斯特德跟我们分享这些时，我心想，天哪，我完全不知道。

1359
01:06:50.410 --> 01:06:51.250
This is the thing.
关键就在这儿。

1360
01:06:51.330 --> 01:06:59.430
When you don't work on the same day as your fellow actors, I had no idea this whole time that John was running up a flight of stairs for every take.
当你和搭档演员不在同一天工作时，我一直都不知道约翰为了每一个镜头都要跑上一层楼梯。

1361
01:06:59.650 --> 01:07:00.150
I know.
我知道。

1362
01:07:00.150 --> 01:07:09.390
Well, Dwight, Jim, and Harry are all going to stumble into the prestige offices, and they're going to find out it's too late.
嗯，德怀特、吉姆和哈里都要闯进高级办公室，他们会发现已经太晚了。

1363
01:07:09.730 --> 01:07:13.250
Mr. Ramesh has already signed with Big Red Paper Company.
拉梅什先生已经和红纸公司签约了。

1364
01:07:13.510 --> 01:07:17.290
We got a really fun piece of fan mail about this scene.
我们收到了一封关于这场戏的非常有趣的粉丝来信。

1365
01:07:17.290 --> 01:07:18.830
It's from Stacey B.
来自威斯康星州的斯泰西·B。

1366
01:07:19.090 --> 01:07:20.930
in Wisconsin, who says,
她写道：

1367
01:07:21.170 --> 01:07:25.750
My 11-year-old daughter has been waiting to submit a fan catch.
我11岁的女儿一直等着提交一个粉丝发现。

1368
01:07:26.070 --> 01:07:32.210
When Jim and Dwight get to the prestige offices, Mr. Ramesh is holding an orange ball.
当吉姆和德怀特到达高级办公室时，拉梅什先生手里拿着一个橙色的球。

1369
01:07:32.710 --> 01:07:34.930
But later in the scene, it's blue.
但在那场戏的后面，它变成了蓝色的。

1370
01:07:35.410 --> 01:07:40.750
My 14-year-old son thinks that the ball has two different sides, one of each color.
我14岁的儿子认为那个球有两个不同的面，一面一个颜色。

1371
01:07:40.750 --> 01:07:49.170
Well, Stacey, first of all, big props to your daughter, because I went back and rewatched the scene, and I saw exactly what she saw.
嗯，斯泰西，首先，要大大表扬一下你的女儿，因为我回去重看了那场戏，我看到了她所看到的一切。

1372
01:07:49.310 --> 01:07:53.030
In one shot, he's holding an orange ball, and then he's holding a blue ball.
在一个镜头里，他拿着一个橙色的球，然后他又拿着一个蓝色的球。

1373
01:07:53.790 --> 01:07:56.990
And shout out to your son, who is right.
也要向你的儿子致敬，他是对的。

1374
01:07:57.310 --> 01:08:00.190
It is a two-sided ball.
那确实是一个双面球。

1375
01:08:00.590 --> 01:08:00.910
It is.
没错。

1376
01:08:00.910 --> 01:08:05.330
You can see both sides very briefly at 15 minutes and 19 seconds.
在15分19秒的时候，你可以非常短暂地看到两面。

1377
01:08:05.330 --> 01:08:11.410
The side facing Mr. Ramesh is orange, and the side facing Jim and Dwight and Harry is blue.
朝向拉梅什先生的那面是橙色的，而朝向吉姆、德怀特和哈里的那面是蓝色的。

1378
01:08:11.810 --> 01:08:12.810
Great catch.
发现得太棒了。

1379
01:08:13.030 --> 01:08:14.090
Great catch.
发现得太棒了。

1380
01:08:14.270 --> 01:08:15.910
I would like to throw this out there.
我想提一点。

1381
01:08:16.290 --> 01:08:16.770
Yeah?
是吗？

1382
01:08:17.470 --> 01:08:20.910
Syracuse University, their colors are orange and blue.
雪城大学，他们的校色就是橙色和蓝色。

1383
01:08:21.550 --> 01:08:22.190
Hey.
嘿。

1384
01:08:22.630 --> 01:08:23.090
Hey.
嘿。

1385
01:08:23.910 --> 01:08:29.130
It looked like a ball, but it also looked like maybe a little football.
它看起来像个球，但也看起来像个小橄榄球。

1386
01:08:29.470 --> 01:08:32.330
It didn't look spherical to me.
在我看来它不是圆形的。

1387
01:08:32.330 --> 01:08:35.110
It looked whatever the shape of a football is.
它看起来就是橄榄球的那种形状。

1388
01:08:35.930 --> 01:08:36.590
That shape.
那种形状。

1389
01:08:37.130 --> 01:08:38.310
A football shape.
橄榄球的形状。

1390
01:08:38.450 --> 01:08:43.010
It looked sporty to me, and I think it's a little nod to Syracuse University.
它看起来很有运动感，我觉得这是对雪城大学的一点致敬。

1391
01:08:43.290 --> 01:08:44.230
It probably was.
很有可能。

1392
01:08:45.070 --> 01:08:54.730
Back at Dunder Mifflin, Scranton, Pam is going to go in the conference room and tell Robert that she stole Nellie's phone, and they're going to listen to the messages together.
回到斯克兰顿的邓德·米夫林，帕姆走进会议室告诉罗伯特她偷了内莉的手机，他们要一起听里面的留言。

1393
01:08:54.990 --> 01:08:55.470
Yes.
是的。

1394
01:08:55.610 --> 01:08:58.990
And they don't paint a great picture of Nellie's life.
这些留言并没有展现出内莉美好的生活。

1395
01:08:59.130 --> 01:09:00.770
It really starts to affect Pam.
这真的开始影响帕姆了。

1396
01:09:01.530 --> 01:09:06.030
Yeah, there's a message from her mom who's just trying to cheer her up.
是的，有一条留言来自她妈妈，只是想让她振作起来。

1397
01:09:06.350 --> 01:09:09.690
The credit card company says she's over her limit.
信用卡公司说她已经超额了。

1398
01:09:09.690 --> 01:09:13.850
Her brother asks if her boss is still hitting on her.
她哥哥问她老板是不是还在骚扰她。

1399
01:09:14.130 --> 01:09:21.990
And then there's a call from an adoption agency rejecting her application to adopt a child.
然后还有一个来自领养机构的电话，拒绝了她的领养申请。

1400
01:09:22.850 --> 01:09:23.830
Pam's heard enough.
帕姆听不下去了。

1401
01:09:24.030 --> 01:09:25.370
She deletes all the messages.
她删除了所有的留言。

1402
01:09:25.670 --> 01:09:28.050
Robert's like, ah, you just messed it all up.
罗伯特当时大概是说，啊，你把一切都搞砸了。

1403
01:09:28.310 --> 01:09:28.970
I know.
我知道。

1404
01:09:29.150 --> 01:09:30.010
Pam's like, ah.
帕姆大概是说，啊。

1405
01:09:30.410 --> 01:09:31.470
That was very funny.
那真的很有趣。

1406
01:09:32.110 --> 01:09:33.490
Fan question from Charlotte H.
来自夏洛特·H的粉丝提问。

1407
01:09:33.670 --> 01:09:34.310
in England.
来自英国。

1408
01:09:35.150 --> 01:09:41.190
Charlotte would like to know who plays Nellie's mom and brother on her voicemail, and are they actually British?
夏洛特想知道是谁在奈莉的语音留言里扮演了她的妈妈和哥哥，他们真的是英国人吗？

1409
01:09:41.590 --> 01:09:50.070
Well, Charlotte, Nellie's mom's voice was played by our stand-in Lori Sox, who is not British, but who did a very good job on this phone call.
嗯，夏洛特，奈莉妈妈的声音是由我们的替身演员洛里·索克斯扮演的，她不是英国人，但她在那个电话里表现得非常出色。

1410
01:09:50.190 --> 01:09:54.570
And I wasn't able to figure out whose voices were on the rest of the messages.
至于其余留言里的声音，我没能查出来是谁。

1411
01:09:54.770 --> 01:09:59.290
Steve Burgess said we hired voice performers, but he didn't have any details on who they were anymore.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说我们雇佣了配音演员，但他已经不记得具体是谁了。

1412
01:09:59.290 --> 01:10:09.710
Yeah, and I asked Danny about the voice of the brother because I saw an online theory that it was Mackenzie Crook, who played Gareth in the BBC version of The Office.
是的，我问过丹尼关于那个哥哥的声音，因为我在网上看到一种理论，说那是麦肯齐·克鲁克，也就是BBC版《办公室》里加雷斯的扮演者。

1413
01:10:10.090 --> 01:10:12.810
But Danny said, no, he didn't think so.
但丹尼说，不，他不这么认为。

1414
01:10:12.890 --> 01:10:16.530
He said if that was the case, they feel like they would have made it more of a thing.
他说如果真是那样的话，他们觉得应该会把这件事大肆宣传一番。

1415
01:10:16.830 --> 01:10:17.630
For sure.
确实。

1416
01:10:17.870 --> 01:10:19.590
He debunked that theory.
他推翻了那个理论。

1417
01:10:20.010 --> 01:10:23.650
Well, Pam is now going to go into Nellie's office and return her cell phone.
好了，帕姆现在要走进奈莉的办公室把手机还给她。

1418
01:10:24.210 --> 01:10:25.770
And Nellie is shopping.
奈莉正在购物。

1419
01:10:26.070 --> 01:10:27.310
She's looking at some sandals.
她在看凉鞋。

1420
01:10:28.350 --> 01:10:30.250
She wants to buy Pam a pair.
她想给帕姆买一双。

1421
01:10:31.490 --> 01:10:33.530
And they have this really sweet moment.
她们在那一刻真的很温馨。

1422
01:10:34.430 --> 01:10:34.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1423
01:10:35.070 --> 01:10:38.470
Nellie sort of seems like she's going to finally share the details of this message.
奈莉看起来好像终于要分享这条留言的细节了。

1424
01:10:38.570 --> 01:10:40.090
And Pam is almost stopping her.
而帕姆几乎在阻止她。

1425
01:10:40.230 --> 01:10:41.130
Like, I don't want to know.
就像是，我不想知道。

1426
01:10:41.310 --> 01:10:42.750
You don't have to talk about it.
你不必谈论它。

1427
01:10:43.010 --> 01:10:45.910
And they do end up bonding sort of sweetly.
她们最终确实建立了一种温馨的联系。

1428
01:10:46.530 --> 01:10:50.170
And Nellie has a talking head where she says things are really looking up.
奈莉有一个采访镜头，她说事情真的在好转。

1429
01:10:50.470 --> 01:10:52.490
You know, she might be a mother soon.
你知道，她可能很快就要当妈妈了。

1430
01:10:52.490 --> 01:10:56.030
And she has MasterCard just where she wants them.
而且她已经把万事达卡拿捏得死死的。

1431
01:10:56.150 --> 01:10:58.350
And now she has a new friend at work.
现在她在工作中也有了新朋友。

1432
01:10:58.870 --> 01:11:06.590
You know, Warren and Halstead said that being able to listen to Nellie's messages gave them an opportunity to add layers to her character.
你知道，沃伦和霍尔斯特德说，能够听到奈莉的留言让他们有机会为她的角色增加层次感。

1433
01:11:06.590 --> 01:11:14.810
They said it was always really fun to explore what characters were like outside of the office, what their aspirations were, what their life was about.
他们说探索角色在办公室之外的样子，他们的抱负是什么，他们的生活是怎样的，这总是非常有趣。

1434
01:11:15.150 --> 01:11:21.210
And learning about Nellie's desire to adopt a baby, it really grounded her, gave her some depth.
了解奈莉想要领养孩子的愿望，真的让她变得更真实，赋予了她深度。

1435
01:11:21.390 --> 01:11:25.510
And at this point, we knew that Catherine Tate would be returning next year.
在这一点上，我们知道凯瑟琳·塔特明年会回归。

1436
01:11:25.510 --> 01:11:30.070
And they were planting seeds for her storyline in Season 9.
他们是在为她在第九季的剧情埋下伏笔。

1437
01:11:30.770 --> 01:11:30.970
Yeah.
是的。

1438
01:11:31.290 --> 01:11:33.350
I like seeing this side of Nellie.
我喜欢看到奈莉的这一面。

1439
01:11:33.490 --> 01:11:34.810
I feel like I needed to see it.
我觉得我需要看到这一面。

1440
01:11:35.470 --> 01:11:36.550
Yeah, me too.
是啊，我也是。

1441
01:11:36.870 --> 01:11:44.290
And she's so good when she has these moments, when she talked about her magician ex-boyfriend.
当她有这些时刻时，她表现得太棒了，就像她谈论那个魔术师前男友的时候。

1442
01:11:44.730 --> 01:11:44.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1443
01:11:45.310 --> 01:11:47.390
Like, Catherine Tate can do it all.
凯瑟琳·塔特真是全能。

1444
01:11:47.930 --> 01:11:48.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1445
01:11:49.050 --> 01:11:55.290
Erin is now going to tell Robert that he has a phone call, someone named Salvation, no last name.
艾琳现在要去告诉罗伯特他有一个电话，对方叫“救赎”，没有姓氏。

1446
01:11:56.110 --> 01:11:58.050
Robert answers, and it's Andy.
罗伯特接了电话，是安迪。

1447
01:11:58.330 --> 01:12:00.030
He has called to taunt him.
他打电话来嘲讽他。

1448
01:12:00.670 --> 01:12:10.230
Andy says, hey, the biggest loser in the office just signed the biggest client, so you can either hire me back and get prestigious business back, or he'll find another buyer.
安迪说，嘿，办公室里最大的失败者刚刚签下了最大的客户，所以你要么把我雇回去，重新获得尊贵的业务，要么他会去找别的买家。

1449
01:12:10.830 --> 01:12:13.070
Oh, this does not sit well with Robert.
哦，这让罗伯特很不爽。

1450
01:12:13.830 --> 01:12:15.710
Robert does not care for this.
罗伯特可不吃这一套。

1451
01:12:16.110 --> 01:12:17.730
He goes on the offensive.
他开始反击了。

1452
01:12:18.050 --> 01:12:23.230
He says if Andy wants a street fight, he has no idea how ugly it can get.
他说如果安迪想打街头架，那安迪根本不知道这事儿能有多难看。

1453
01:12:23.680 --> 01:12:25.610
He says, you don't even know my real name.
他说，你甚至都不知道我的真名。

1454
01:12:25.790 --> 01:12:27.310
I'm the f***ing Lizard King.
我可是他妈的蜥蜴之王。

1455
01:12:28.090 --> 01:12:28.630
What?
什么？

1456
01:12:29.130 --> 01:12:29.710
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1457
01:12:30.710 --> 01:12:31.250
Whoa.
哇。

1458
01:12:31.830 --> 01:12:33.710
This was a fan mail flurry, lady.
这可是粉丝来信大爆发啊，女士。

1459
01:12:34.170 --> 01:12:34.790
Anna W.
来自南卡罗来纳州的安娜·W.

1460
01:12:35.070 --> 01:12:38.230
from South Carolina said, I've been waiting to ask this question.
说，我一直等着问这个问题。

1461
01:12:38.770 --> 01:12:44.370
I'm 32 years old, and everywhere I see people quoting this line, I'm the f***ing Lizard King.
我今年32岁了，到处都能看到人们引用这句台词：我可是他妈的蜥蜴之王。

1462
01:12:44.650 --> 01:12:45.810
I don't get it.
我不明白。

1463
01:12:45.930 --> 01:12:47.230
I don't understand it.
我理解不了。

1464
01:12:47.530 --> 01:12:48.350
Please help.
请帮帮我。

1465
01:12:48.750 --> 01:12:49.530
Gabe S.
来自旧金山的盖比·S.

1466
01:12:49.750 --> 01:12:55.470
from San Francisco said, this is one of the most underrated office quotes, but one of my favorites.
说，这是《办公室》里最被低估的台词之一，但也是我最喜欢的台词之一。

1467
01:12:55.770 --> 01:12:58.670
Please give more details on how this quote came to be.
请详细讲讲这句台词是怎么来的。

1468
01:12:58.670 --> 01:13:00.110
And Andrea B.
还有来自加拿大安大略省汉密尔顿的安德烈亚·B.

1469
01:13:00.370 --> 01:13:07.930
from Hamilton, Ontario, Canada said, do you know why the writers had Robert California call himself the f***ing Lizard King?
说，你知道为什么编剧要让罗伯特·加州自称“他妈的蜥蜴之王”吗？

1470
01:13:08.250 --> 01:13:15.170
Is this a reference to the Doors song, I am the Lizard King, or to Jim Morrison's same nickname?
这是在致敬大门乐队的歌《我是蜥蜴之王》，还是致敬吉姆·莫里森的同名绰号？

1471
01:13:16.190 --> 01:13:25.200
Well, everyone, we asked Warren and Halstead about this, and Angela, this was just a small amount of the mail that we got on this subject.
各位，我们问过沃伦和霍尔斯特德了，安吉拉，这还只是我们收到的关于这个话题的一小部分来信。

1472
01:13:26.250 --> 01:13:26.570
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1473
01:13:27.290 --> 01:13:32.190
Warren and Halstead said, there was no deep thinking about this in the writers' room.
沃伦和霍尔斯特德说，编剧室里并没有对这个梗进行什么深思熟虑。

1474
01:13:32.190 --> 01:13:35.070
It was just a room pitch that made everyone laugh.
这只是当时在房间里随口一说，结果把大家都逗乐了。

1475
01:13:35.470 --> 01:13:39.530
You know, sometimes the writers would do what's called a punch-up pass on a script.
你知道，有时候编剧会对剧本进行所谓的“润色”。

1476
01:13:39.530 --> 01:13:48.910
It's where they sit around the conference room table, and they read through the script all together as a group, and people can just shout out extra jokes as they go along.
就是大家围坐在会议桌旁，一起通读剧本，过程中大家可以随时喊出额外的笑话。

1477
01:13:49.370 --> 01:13:56.150
And so this was just a shout-out room pitch, and everybody laughed at this idea, and it made it in.
所以这只是当时随口喊出的一个点子，大家都觉得这个主意很有趣，于是就用上了。

1478
01:13:56.510 --> 01:14:01.730
Well, to all the folks that wrote in about this line, I was super curious about it, too.
好吧，对于所有写信问这句台词的朋友们，其实我也超级好奇。

1479
01:14:01.730 --> 01:14:08.810
I was wondering, as well, if maybe Robert California was referencing the song Celebration of the Lizard.
我也在想，罗伯特·加州是不是在引用《蜥蜴的庆典》这首歌。

1480
01:14:09.090 --> 01:14:12.510
The lyrics were by Jim Morrison, the music by The Doors.
歌词是吉姆·莫里森写的，音乐是大门乐队做的。

1481
01:14:12.510 --> 01:14:14.810
I have a clip of it if you'd like to hear it.
如果你想听的话，我这里有一段剪辑。

1482
01:14:14.970 --> 01:14:15.490
Please.
请放吧。

1483
01:14:16.010 --> 01:14:16.890
Here it is.
在这儿。

1484
01:14:16.990 --> 01:14:18.610
It's a very long song.
这首歌很长。

1485
01:14:18.850 --> 01:14:21.210
I think it's 17 minutes and 10 seconds.
我想有17分10秒长。

1486
01:14:22.350 --> 01:14:23.330
The Doors?
大门乐队？

1487
01:14:23.330 --> 01:14:24.290
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

1488
01:14:24.610 --> 01:14:28.750
But at the end, Jim Morrison just sort of starts talking.
但在最后，吉姆·莫里森就开始自顾自地说话了。

1489
01:14:29.130 --> 01:14:29.890
Here it is.
就是这段。

1490
01:14:36.070 --> 01:14:37.670
I am the Lizard King.
我是蜥蜴之王。

1491
01:14:40.640 --> 01:14:44.320
Retire now to your tents and to your dreaMs.
现在退回你们的帐篷，进入你们的梦乡。

1492
01:14:48.800 --> 01:14:51.140
Tomorrow we enter the town of my birth.
明天我们将进入我出生的城镇。

1493
01:14:54.890 --> 01:14:56.250
I want to be ready.
我想做好准备。

1494
01:14:59.870 --> 01:15:02.930
Oh, I mean, kind of tracks with Robert.
哦，我的意思是，这和罗伯特的人设还挺像的。

1495
01:15:03.310 --> 01:15:06.050
Sounds like Robert maybe has listened to this, in my opinion.
依我看，听起来罗伯特可能真的听过这首歌。

1496
01:15:06.310 --> 01:15:13.630
Is it true that Jim Morrison claimed that he could talk to lizards and control them with his mind,
吉姆·莫里森声称他能和蜥蜴对话并用意念控制它们，这是真的吗？

1497
01:15:13.630 --> 01:15:16.230
and that's why he called himself the Lizard King?
这就是他自称蜥蜴之王的原因吗？

1498
01:15:16.550 --> 01:15:22.210
Is this maybe Robert California's belief that he can control others with his mind?
这会不会是罗伯特·加州认为他能用意念控制他人？

1499
01:15:22.210 --> 01:15:24.190
Is that what we're getting at here?
我们想表达的是这个意思吗？

1500
01:15:25.210 --> 01:15:25.730
Maybe.
也许吧。

1501
01:15:25.970 --> 01:15:27.690
I don't know any of that.
那些我一概不知。

1502
01:15:27.930 --> 01:15:32.850
I will say I think Robert California is probably someone who has researched the reptilian brain,
但我得说，我觉得罗伯特·加利福尼亚大概是个研究过爬虫脑的人，

1503
01:15:33.170 --> 01:15:35.970
what that brings out in men, etc.
研究过它如何激发男人的本能等等。

1504
01:15:35.970 --> 01:15:43.010
I'm also pretty sure that Robert California is someone who has listened to an entire 17-minute Doors song.
我还相当确定，罗伯特·加利福尼亚是个会完整听完一首17分钟大门乐队歌曲的人。

1505
01:15:43.410 --> 01:15:45.310
17 minutes and 10 seconds.
17分10秒。

1506
01:15:45.310 --> 01:15:51.070
I think that if you want to persuade someone to stay off drugs,
我觉得如果你想劝人远离毒品，

1507
01:15:51.350 --> 01:15:54.590
you could maybe play the end of this song for them,
或许可以给他们放这首歌的结尾，

1508
01:15:54.750 --> 01:15:59.330
because it sounds like a person who has done too many drugs to me.
因为在我听来，那就像是一个嗑药过量的人发出的声音。

1509
01:16:00.530 --> 01:16:02.590
Don't do drugs, everyone.
大家千万别碰毒品。

1510
01:16:03.310 --> 01:16:04.230
Don't vape.
别抽电子烟。

1511
01:16:04.750 --> 01:16:05.570
Stop the vaping.
停止抽电子烟吧。

1512
01:16:05.710 --> 01:16:06.710
It's not good for you.
这对你没好处。

1513
01:16:07.130 --> 01:16:08.770
Vaping is smoking, right?
电子烟就是吸烟，对吧？

1514
01:16:09.210 --> 01:16:10.010
It's worse.
甚至更糟。

1515
01:16:10.330 --> 01:16:12.850
It creates crystals on your lungs.
它会在你的肺部形成结晶。

1516
01:16:13.010 --> 01:16:14.610
It really destroys your lungs.
它真的会摧毁你的肺。

1517
01:16:14.730 --> 01:16:18.650
It was like, you know, the idea was that it was better, but it's not better.
起初人们以为它更好，但其实不然。

1518
01:16:18.670 --> 01:16:19.570
It's awful.
它糟透了。

1519
01:16:19.570 --> 01:16:22.290
It can lead to strokes at a very young age.
它会导致人在很年轻的时候就中风。

1520
01:16:22.770 --> 01:16:24.570
People are terribly sick from it.
很多人因此病得非常严重。

1521
01:16:24.770 --> 01:16:25.210
Stop it.
停下来吧。

1522
01:16:25.530 --> 01:16:26.290
Stop with the vaping.
别再抽电子烟了。

1523
01:16:26.430 --> 01:16:29.450
Also, it's like it comes in like flavors and stuff.
而且它还有各种口味什么的。

1524
01:16:29.590 --> 01:16:30.690
It just don't do it.
总之别碰它。

1525
01:16:30.930 --> 01:16:32.350
Stop doing it, everyone.
大家都别再抽了。

1526
01:16:33.010 --> 01:16:33.990
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1527
01:16:34.310 --> 01:16:36.190
I'm going to put this in my diet book.
我要把它写进我的减肥书里。

1528
01:16:36.190 --> 01:16:39.190
Oh, your diet book that I've titled Don't Be an Idiot?
哦，就是你那本我命名为《别当白痴》的减肥书？

1529
01:16:39.390 --> 01:16:39.770
Yeah.
没错。

1530
01:16:40.150 --> 01:16:42.830
And it's going to have a section on don't vape either.
里面还会专门加一章劝人别抽电子烟。

1531
01:16:43.330 --> 01:16:45.270
You are ready for your 50s.
你已经准备好迎接50岁的生活了。

1532
01:16:45.350 --> 01:16:46.610
I really am.
我确实准备好了。

1533
01:16:46.750 --> 01:16:47.470
You really are.
你确实是。

1534
01:16:47.950 --> 01:16:49.170
No nonsense.
绝不废话。

1535
01:16:49.170 --> 01:16:50.890
I don't have time for the nonsense.
我没时间废话。

1536
01:16:52.090 --> 01:16:53.010
No time.
没时间。

1537
01:16:53.350 --> 01:16:56.330
Hey, we also got a fan catch from Olivia S.
嘿，我们还收到了一位来自华盛顿州西雅图的粉丝奥利维亚·S的反馈。

1538
01:16:56.390 --> 01:16:59.910
in Seattle, Washington, who had a lip flap catch.
她发现了一个口型对不上的地方。

1539
01:17:00.650 --> 01:17:04.210
Olivia said, is it just me or does Robert California say,
奥利维亚问，是我多心了还是罗伯特·加利福尼亚确实说了，

1540
01:17:04.210 --> 01:17:06.430
I am the mother effing Lizard King.
“我是他妈的蜥蜴王”。

1541
01:17:06.950 --> 01:17:10.650
And not only does it show a lip flap, but it is not bleeped.
而且不仅口型对不上，还没有被消音。

1542
01:17:11.130 --> 01:17:13.550
How did this slip through standards and practices?
这怎么能逃过审查部门的眼睛呢？

1543
01:17:14.350 --> 01:17:20.630
Olivia, I don't know what version you were watching, but mine is fully blurred and fully bleeped.
奥利维亚，我不知道你看的是哪个版本，但我这边的版本是完全模糊处理且完全消音的。

1544
01:17:21.210 --> 01:17:22.230
Steve Burgess said,
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，

1545
01:17:22.230 --> 01:17:25.670
The only note from standards and practices was this.
审查部门唯一的批注是这个。

1546
01:17:26.050 --> 01:17:33.570
As previously noted, please blur Robert's lip flap when he says, quote, f***ing to Andy on the phone.
如前所述，请在罗伯特对安迪说“他妈的”时，对他的口型进行模糊处理。

1547
01:17:33.850 --> 01:17:39.610
So no reference in the script or from standards and practices for mother effing.
所以剧本里或审查部门并没有提到“他妈的”这个词。

1548
01:17:40.130 --> 01:17:43.650
And my lip flap was blurred and bleeped.
而且我的口型确实被模糊处理并消音了。

1549
01:17:43.990 --> 01:17:47.190
Olivia, what version of this episode do you have?
奥利维亚，你到底看的是哪一版的剧集？

1550
01:17:47.810 --> 01:17:53.470
Well, I will also share that in the shooting draft, it is just, I'm the f***ing Lizard King.
好吧，我还要分享一下，在拍摄剧本里，那句台词只是“我是他妈的蜥蜴王”。

1551
01:17:53.630 --> 01:17:54.470
So there's no mother.
所以没有母亲。

1552
01:17:54.770 --> 01:17:55.470
No mother.
没有母亲。

1553
01:17:55.750 --> 01:17:56.410
No mother.
没有母亲。

1554
01:17:57.050 --> 01:17:57.530
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1555
01:17:57.930 --> 01:17:59.650
We're going to have a big twist now.
我们现在要迎来一个大反转了。

1556
01:18:00.210 --> 01:18:01.330
Andy gets out of his car.
安迪下了车。

1557
01:18:01.510 --> 01:18:05.330
He walks up to a very famous green door, knocks on it.
他走到一扇非常有名的绿色大门前，敲了敲门。

1558
01:18:05.510 --> 01:18:06.550
Guess who's inside?
猜猜里面是谁？

1559
01:18:06.750 --> 01:18:08.250
It's David Wallace's house.
是大卫·华莱士的家。

1560
01:18:08.710 --> 01:18:11.170
Yes, I love that this is who Andy went to.
没错，我喜欢安迪去找他这个设定。

1561
01:18:11.270 --> 01:18:16.970
I felt like they had planted that seed in fundraiser when the two of them had their conversation outside of the bathroom.
我觉得他们在筹款活动那集，两人在洗手间外谈话时就已经埋下伏笔了。

1562
01:18:17.190 --> 01:18:17.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1563
01:18:18.290 --> 01:18:23.950
David Wallace answers the door and Andy says, would you like to invest in a fledgling paper company?
大卫·华莱士开了门，安迪说，你愿意投资一家刚起步的造纸公司吗？

1564
01:18:24.230 --> 01:18:28.570
Under the right management, it could be worth twice than what he would pay for it today.
在正确的管理下，它的价值可能会翻倍，远超他今天投入的成本。

1565
01:18:29.030 --> 01:18:31.010
David Wallace says, come on inside.
大卫·华莱士说，进来吧。

1566
01:18:31.790 --> 01:18:32.350
Dun, dun, dun.
当当当。

1567
01:18:33.170 --> 01:18:35.250
We had a fan question from Jessica N.
我们收到一个来自纽约罗切斯特的粉丝杰西卡·N的提问，她说在本集结尾，

1568
01:18:35.310 --> 01:18:38.190
in Rochester, New York, who said at the end of this episode,
大卫·华莱士的房子看起来和前几季的不一样。

1569
01:18:38.430 --> 01:18:43.650
it doesn't look like David Wallace's house is the same house from the previous seasons.
没错，它确实有一扇绿色的门，但看起来像是坐落在拐角处。

1570
01:18:44.170 --> 01:18:48.230
Yes, it has a green door, but it looks like it's sitting on a corner lot.
房子的左侧似乎有更多的空地。

1571
01:18:48.470 --> 01:18:51.990
There seems like there's a lot more open space to the left of this house.
杰西卡说，我没时间回去看前几季的剧集，

1572
01:18:52.510 --> 01:18:56.150
Jessica said, I didn't have time to look back at the previous season episodes,
但我上网搜了一下，发现那栋真正的房子几年前在出售，

1573
01:18:56.150 --> 01:19:01.530
but when I searched it online, I discovered that the actual house was for sale a few years ago
而且当时引发了一场相当激烈的竞价战。

1574
01:19:01.530 --> 01:19:03.510
and there was quite a bidding war over it.
好吧，观察得很仔细，杰西卡。

1575
01:19:03.890 --> 01:19:05.190
Well, good catch, Jessica.
没错，你简直是妈妈侦探附体。

1576
01:19:05.190 --> 01:19:07.990
Yeah, you totally mom-detective this.
她有一些很棒的理论。

1577
01:19:08.150 --> 01:19:09.650
She has some great theories.
她做了一些调查，但我们目前还没有确切的答案。

1578
01:19:09.650 --> 01:19:12.690
She's done a little bit of digging, but we don't have a real answer.
好吧，她启发了我。

1579
01:19:12.990 --> 01:19:14.450
Well, she got me started.
杰西卡，我们第一季用的大卫·华莱士的家是在帕萨迪纳。

1580
01:19:15.290 --> 01:19:19.910
Jessica, the first house we used for David Wallace's house was in Pasadena.
这栋房子是在恩西诺。

1581
01:19:20.190 --> 01:19:21.970
This house was in Encino.
它们是两栋不同的房子。

1582
01:19:22.130 --> 01:19:23.550
They are two different houses.
而且正如你所说，最初那栋帕萨迪纳的房子在2021年上市了。

1583
01:19:23.550 --> 01:19:28.710
And, like you said, the original Pasadena house went on the market in 2021.
它确实引发了一场巨大的竞价战。

1584
01:19:28.850 --> 01:19:31.370
It did spark a huge bidding war.
这栋房子最终以超过600万美元的要价成交了。

1585
01:19:31.570 --> 01:19:36.630
The house eventually sold for over its $6 million asking price.
哇哦。

1586
01:19:36.910 --> 01:19:37.590
Cha-ching.
我发现了一个名叫“Rob on Location”的博主。

1587
01:19:38.510 --> 01:19:42.610
I found a blogger by the name of Rob on Location.
他对我们所有的拍摄地点都有详尽的分析。

1588
01:19:42.770 --> 01:19:45.810
He has an extensive breakdown of all of our locations.
他参观过大卫·华莱士的两处住所。

1589
01:19:45.810 --> 01:19:50.670
And he has visited both of David Wallace's homes.
你猜怎么着？

1590
01:19:51.030 --> 01:19:52.050
And guess what?
当他在2023年6月参观最初那栋帕萨迪纳的房子时，

1591
01:19:52.530 --> 01:19:56.270
When he visited the original Pasadena house in June of 2023,
它已经被彻底拆空了。

1592
01:19:56.270 --> 01:19:59.430
it had been completely gutted.
彻底拆光了。

1593
01:19:59.890 --> 01:20:00.890
Completely lady.
就像整个外立面都没了。

1594
01:20:01.170 --> 01:20:03.050
Like the whole facade.
只剩下框架？

1595
01:20:03.350 --> 01:20:04.350
Save the framing?
是的。

1596
01:20:04.690 --> 01:20:05.310
Yes.
这也意味着他们花了超过600万美元买下它，然后基本上把它拆了。

1597
01:20:05.550 --> 01:20:11.710
Also, that means that they paid over $6 million for it and then basically tore it down.
我不明白。

1598
01:20:11.710 --> 01:20:12.750
I don't get it.
我不明白。

1599
01:20:12.910 --> 01:20:13.850
I don't get it.
简直疯了。

1600
01:20:14.090 --> 01:20:14.810
Bonkers.
太疯狂了。

1601
01:20:15.450 --> 01:20:20.710
And then he had visited the Encino house in 2022, and it was also under renovation.
后来他在2022年参观了恩西诺的那栋房子，当时房子也在翻修。

1602
01:20:20.710 --> 01:20:21.750
He has photos.
他有照片。

1603
01:20:22.210 --> 01:20:25.170
Angela, I'll give you the website for Office Lady Stories.
安吉拉，我会把“办公室女士故事”的网站发给你。

1604
01:20:25.730 --> 01:20:26.250
Okay.
好的。

1605
01:20:26.970 --> 01:20:27.870
Rob on Location.
外景拍摄的罗伯。

1606
01:20:28.090 --> 01:20:31.090
But anyway, Jessica, you were right.
但不管怎样，杰西卡，你是对的。

1607
01:20:31.510 --> 01:20:32.870
It's not the same house.
那不是同一栋房子。

1608
01:20:33.110 --> 01:20:33.770
Two different houses.
是两栋不同的房子。

1609
01:20:34.350 --> 01:20:39.870
Well, this episode is going to end with our three failed salesmen, Harry, Jim, and Dwight.
嗯，这一集将以我们三位失败的推销员——哈里、吉姆和德怀特——的场景结束。

1610
01:20:39.990 --> 01:20:44.010
They've gotten coffee, and now they're just kind of hanging out and talking.
他们买了咖啡，现在正聚在一起闲聊。

1611
01:20:44.810 --> 01:20:48.170
Harry's going to ask the guys what they would do if they weren't paper salesmen.
哈里问大家如果不是做纸张推销员，他们会做什么。

1612
01:20:48.450 --> 01:20:55.550
He says that he would like to sell one big thing, one huge sale, like an airplane.
他说他想做一笔大生意，那种超级大单，比如卖飞机。

1613
01:20:56.570 --> 01:20:57.690
And then he's out.
然后他就收手了。

1614
01:20:58.050 --> 01:21:04.830
And he also tells them he thinks Robert is going to run Dunder Mifflin into the ground, and they won't even be doing this in six months anyway.
他还告诉他们，他觉得罗伯特会把邓德·米夫林公司搞垮，反正六个月后他们可能连这份工作都没了。

1615
01:21:05.290 --> 01:21:05.510
Yeah.
没错。

1616
01:21:05.690 --> 01:21:12.410
He sort of implies you better be thinking about what you're going to do if you weren't a paper salesman, because you probably aren't going to be one for long.
他暗示大家最好考虑一下如果不做纸张推销员该干什么，因为这份工作他们大概干不长了。

1617
01:21:12.810 --> 01:21:16.430
Well, you know, I love a callback, and Jim has one in this scene.
嗯，你知道的，我喜欢这种前后呼应，吉姆在这一幕里就有一个。

1618
01:21:16.590 --> 01:21:18.350
He says he'd like to own a bike shop.
他说他想开一家自行车店。

1619
01:21:19.010 --> 01:21:19.190
Yeah.
没错。

1620
01:21:19.830 --> 01:21:29.030
And this reminded me of the episode Lotto, where Jim says he'd probably buy a big piece of land in Maine, build a house, work in town, somewhere I could bike to or kayak to.
这让我想起了《彩票》那一集，吉姆说他可能会在缅因州买一大块地，盖栋房子，在镇上工作，去哪里都能骑车或划皮划艇到达。

1621
01:21:29.170 --> 01:21:33.130
I'd either bike to my job at the kayak shop or kayak to my job at the bike shop.
我要么骑车去皮划艇店上班，要么划皮划艇去自行车店上班。

1622
01:21:33.390 --> 01:21:36.870
I asked Warren if this callback was intentional, and here's what they had to say.
我问了沃伦这个呼应是不是故意的，他是这么说的。

1623
01:21:36.870 --> 01:21:43.390
They said they didn't want the conversation to be too serious, which is why they start with a joke from Jim at Dwight's expense.
他们说不想让谈话显得太严肃，所以他们先用吉姆拿德怀特开玩笑的话题开了个头。

1624
01:21:43.990 --> 01:21:49.590
But Jim's bike shop idea was definitely intentional and something they talked a lot about in the writer's room.
但吉姆想开自行车店的想法绝对是刻意安排的，也是他们在编剧室讨论过很多次的内容。

1625
01:21:50.630 --> 01:21:57.410
Well, Danny Chun said he especially loved this scene at the end of the episode out on the grass outside the office building.
嗯，丹尼·春说他特别喜欢这一集结尾在办公楼外草地上的那一幕。

1626
01:21:57.750 --> 01:22:03.270
He said it felt very grounded and real, and a lot of that was because of Chris Bauer playing it so real.
他说那一幕感觉非常扎实、真实，很大程度上是因为克里斯·鲍尔演得太真实了。

1627
01:22:03.270 --> 01:22:13.050
Well, Warren and Halstead said they also just loved having plot lines in general with Rain and John together, similar to their script After Hours with the bedbugs.
嗯，沃伦和霍尔斯特德说他们也特别喜欢让雷恩和约翰在一起演对手戏，就像他们写的《加班》里关于臭虫的那段戏一样。

1628
01:22:13.330 --> 01:22:23.830
Warren said that he and Halstead would often approach Jim Dwight scenes as if they were a buddy cop movie, where both cops want the same goal,
沃伦说他和霍尔斯特德经常把吉姆和德怀特的对手戏处理成那种“搭档警探”电影的风格，两个警察目标一致，

1629
01:22:23.970 --> 01:22:28.670
but their methods to achieving that goal are always fraught with squabbling and misunderstandings.
但他们实现目标的方法总是充满了争吵和误解。

1630
01:22:28.670 --> 01:22:37.470
But in the end, they have a bit of a friendship, and I thought that was just such a fun way to explain Jim and Dwight, especially in this episode.
但最终，他们之间产生了一点友谊，我觉得用这种方式来解读吉姆和德怀特非常有趣，尤其是在这一集里。

1631
01:22:37.970 --> 01:22:38.930
Yeah, I love that.
没错，我很喜欢这一点。

1632
01:22:39.110 --> 01:22:42.710
I want to watch episodes now with that information in my brain.
我现在想带着这个信息再看一遍这些剧集。

1633
01:22:43.530 --> 01:22:47.650
Well, you know, this wouldn't have been the final scene in the shooting draft.
嗯，你知道，这本来不会是拍摄初稿里的最后一幕。

1634
01:22:47.790 --> 01:22:48.670
There was another scene.
还有另一场戏。

1635
01:22:48.670 --> 01:22:53.910
It was a tag, and it was Harry showing the camera crew around Syracuse.
那是一个尾声，是哈里带着摄制组参观雪城分公司。

1636
01:22:54.450 --> 01:22:54.970
What?
什么？

1637
01:22:54.970 --> 01:22:56.710
Yeah, yes.
对，没错。

1638
01:22:57.070 --> 01:22:58.890
Oh my goodness, Rob L.
天哪，罗伯·L。

1639
01:22:59.150 --> 01:23:02.550
There's a deleted scene where we see the Syracuse branch.
有一个删减片段，我们看到了雪城分公司。

1640
01:23:02.990 --> 01:23:06.570
Yes, I guess the camera crew follows Harry back to work.
是的，我想摄制组跟着哈里回到了工作地点。

1641
01:23:06.790 --> 01:23:10.690
It's also in deleted scenes, and I thought we should end the episode with it.
它也在删减片段里，我觉得我们应该用它来结束这一集。

1642
01:23:10.890 --> 01:23:11.850
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

1643
01:23:12.550 --> 01:23:14.910
What's your fascination with the Scranton branch?
你对斯克兰顿分公司有什么迷之执着？

1644
01:23:15.250 --> 01:23:18.070
We got all the same drama and wackadoos as them.
我们这儿的戏剧性和怪人一点也不比他们少。

1645
01:23:18.390 --> 01:23:21.570
This guy Mike, same lunch every day.
这个叫迈克的家伙，每天午餐都吃一样的。

1646
01:23:21.870 --> 01:23:23.490
Chef salad, 15 years.
厨师沙拉，吃了15年了。

1647
01:23:24.630 --> 01:23:28.150
And Janelle, she's an African-American woman working in HR.
还有珍妮尔，她是人力资源部的非裔美国女性。

1648
01:23:28.410 --> 01:23:29.550
She wears wigs.
她戴假发。

1649
01:23:30.270 --> 01:23:31.930
Let's have three, four wigs.
大概有三四顶假发吧。

1650
01:23:32.110 --> 01:23:33.750
Like, what's your hair going to be today?
就像是，你今天打算换什么发型？

1651
01:23:34.010 --> 01:23:34.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

1652
01:23:35.590 --> 01:23:37.050
The audience could get into it.
观众可能会喜欢。

1653
01:23:37.190 --> 01:23:39.930
You know, like, what's it going to be today?
你知道，就像是，今天会发生什么呢？

1654
01:23:40.630 --> 01:23:43.930
I mean, we even got a Pam, too, except her name's Sharon, and she's pretty funny looking.
我的意思是，我们甚至也有个“帕姆”，只不过她叫莎伦，而且她长得挺滑稽的。

1655
01:23:44.410 --> 01:23:47.930
She's in love with this guy, Matt, and he's really ugly, too.
她爱上了一个叫马特的家伙，那家伙也长得特别丑。

1656
01:23:47.930 --> 01:23:52.570
They got kind of a will they, won't they thing going, only everyone's rooting for won't they.
他们之间有点那种“到底会不会在一起”的暧昧，只不过大家都在盼着他们“千万别在一起”。

1657
01:23:52.750 --> 01:23:57.650
I cannot stress enough how unappealing these two individuals are, truly.
我必须强调，这两个人真的非常倒胃口，一点都不夸张。

1658
01:23:57.830 --> 01:23:59.710
If they ever got together, it would destroy your project.
如果他们真的在一起了，那你们的项目就毁了。

1659
01:24:02.670 --> 01:24:10.400
Seeing these people as he's describing a whole montage.
看着他描述整个蒙太奇片段时这些人的样子。

1660
01:24:10.400 --> 01:24:10.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1661
01:24:11.100 --> 01:24:11.600
Oh, my goodness.
我的天呐。

1662
01:24:11.600 --> 01:24:12.620
And you see everybody.
然后你看到了所有人。

1663
01:24:14.820 --> 01:24:15.260
Wow.
哇。

1664
01:24:15.600 --> 01:24:18.180
Well, that is a great way to end this episode.
好吧，这真是结束这一集的绝佳方式。

1665
01:24:18.520 --> 01:24:20.200
Everyone, that was Turf War.
各位，刚才那集是《地盘之争》。

1666
01:24:20.400 --> 01:24:22.720
I have to say, I really enjoyed this one.
我得说，我真的很喜欢这一集。

1667
01:24:23.060 --> 01:24:23.920
I'm going to be honeSt.
老实说。

1668
01:24:23.920 --> 01:24:26.920
I think there have been a few clunkers in season eight.
我觉得第八季里有几集挺烂的。

1669
01:24:27.160 --> 01:24:28.460
This one is not one of them.
但这一集绝对不是其中之一。

1670
01:24:28.460 --> 01:24:29.920
I really, really liked it.
我真的、真的很喜欢它。

1671
01:24:30.700 --> 01:24:34.960
Also, huge thank you to everyone that wrote in with their questions and comments,
另外，非常感谢每一位写信来提问和评论的朋友，

1672
01:24:35.120 --> 01:24:40.040
to Warren and Halstead and Dani for answering all of our questions.
感谢沃伦、霍尔斯特德和丹妮回答了我们所有的问题。

1673
01:24:40.300 --> 01:24:43.940
And also to Steve Burgess and Zach Woods and Rainn Wilson.
还要感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯、扎克·伍兹和雷恩·威尔森。

1674
01:24:44.400 --> 01:24:47.200
Wow, we had a lot of people help us out on this one.
哇，这一集我们得到了很多人的帮助。

1675
01:24:47.520 --> 01:24:48.420
All right, you guys.
好了，各位。

1676
01:24:48.600 --> 01:24:49.380
Have a great week.
祝你们度过愉快的一周。

1677
01:24:49.520 --> 01:24:52.500
We'll be back next week with Free Family Portrait Studio.
下周我们将回来讨论《免费家庭肖像摄影室》。

1678
01:24:52.600 --> 01:24:54.960
The last episode of season eight.
这是第八季的最后一集。

1679
01:24:55.400 --> 01:24:55.680
Ah!
啊！

1680
01:24:56.420 --> 01:24:56.800
All right.
好的。

1681
01:24:56.800 --> 01:24:57.240
See you then.
到时见。

1682
01:24:57.480 --> 01:24:58.300
Have a good one.
祝你们过得愉快。

1683
01:24:58.300 --> 01:25:06.670
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1684
01:25:06.930 --> 01:25:11.070
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1685
01:25:11.270 --> 01:25:13.430
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的高级制作人是卡西·杰金斯。

1686
01:25:13.630 --> 01:25:15.730
Our in-studio engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的演播室工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1687
01:25:15.930 --> 01:25:18.110
Our editing and mixing engineer is Jordan Duffy.
我们的剪辑和混音工程师是乔丹·达菲。

1688
01:25:18.370 --> 01:25:20.450
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubaco.
我们的助理制作人是安斯利·布巴科。

1689
01:25:20.770 --> 01:25:23.590
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿演唱的《橡胶树》。
